Description :

Marsh is seeking candidates for the following position based in Madrid :

Business Analyst / Project Manager

What can you expect?
• The purpose of this role is to play a pivotal role in bridging business stakeholders and technology teams, ensuring alignment between software / system development and business requirements for successful project delivery;
• Contribute to the planning and coordination of projects, carry out administrative responsibilities, and directly manage some crucial components of project management to guarantee projects are finished on schedule.

What is in it for you?
• Opportunity to work in a dynamic and truly global team and role;
• Many development and on-the job learning opportunities;
• Competitive salary and benefits;
• Business casual dress code, integration and wellbeing events;
• Multilingual community with inclusive atmosphere;
• For the initial 6 months it will be required to work from the office. After that, you can opt for the hybrid... working model, which allows you to work from home 2 days per week.

We will count on you to :
• Translate business strategies and objectives into business requirements;
• Identify, verifiy and document functional and operational requirements using requirements management methodology and tools;
• Test and analyze final requirements;
• Ensure requirements are communicated effectively to parties responsible for technical development and implementation;
• Manage data and reporting requests;
• Manage projects and perform follow-ups.

What you need to have :
• Knowledge in general insurance area minimum 2 years;
• Business analyst experience minimum 2 years;
• Project management and organizational skills with the ability to prioritize and manage multiple projects simultaneously;
• Ability to build and sustain strong relationships with internal stakeholders;
• Fluent English level (C1);
• Strong communication and presentation skills;
• Proficient with MS Office and general ease with different systems.
• Project management experience is highly desirable

What makes you stand out :
• Team player combined with the ability to work independently with minimal supervision;
• Good analytical skills and strong attention to details;
• Knowledge and experience in employee benefits (life and health insurance is high desirable).

If you would like to apply for this position, please send in your application in English.

is the world’s leading insurance broker and risk adviser. With over 35, colleagues operating in more than countries, Marsh serves commercial and individual clients with data driven risk solutions and advisory services.

Marsh is a business of (NYSE : MMC), the leading global professional services firm in the areas of risk, strategy and people.

